# Run with: kanso test test_runner_aborts_on_deep_recursion.kso
#
# One test recurses too deep. `kanso run --interp` and `kanso play` report
# this shape cleanly ("error[runtime]: the program ran out of stack"), but the
# test runner aborts the whole process, so no other test's result is
# reported and the exit status is 134.
#
# Should: report test_deep as failed (or as out of stack), report
# test_shallow ... ok, and exit 1.
#
# Does:
#   test_shallow ... ok
#   thread 'main' has overflowed its stack
#   fatal runtime error: stack overflow, aborting        (exit 134)
#
# In the Lox port the same abort comes from a Lox recursion only 700 calls
# deep, while `kanso run --interp` handles 2,000.
fn depth 0
  0

fn depth n
  mix (depth (n - 1)) n

fn mix total n
  total + n % 7

test_shallow = depth 10 == 27

test_deep = depth 1000000 > 0
